WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.400
-It's nice to see you
again, bud.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.701
-Yeah. Good to be back.

00:00:03.701 --> 00:00:05.701
-Yeah, two nights in a row
for you, bud.

00:00:05.701 --> 00:00:07.534
-For sure.
-You've been on the show before.

00:00:07.534 --> 00:00:11.200
By the way, do I call you Pusha?
Do I call you Pusha T?

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.000
-Push is good.
-Pusha? Okay, good.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:14.334
-Push. Push.
-Push?

00:00:14.334 --> 00:00:15.501
-Yeah, Push is good.
-Thank you.

00:00:15.501 --> 00:00:17.000
-You my man.
-Appreciate it. Thanks.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.667
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:20.834
-What do you feel like
calling me, Jimmy or Jim?

00:00:20.834 --> 00:00:22.167
-Jim.
-Yeah.

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:23.667
Okay, good. You can call me Jim.

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:25.000
Alright, Push.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:28.834
Uh, I, uh...
What is, uh...

00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:31.667
Pusha T, what does it --
is there a meaning behind it?

00:00:31.667 --> 00:00:33.000
-Man, you know what?

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Pharrell actually
named me Pusha.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.167
-Pharrell did?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:39.300
You know, we used to be
in the studio a lot,

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:43.133
and I would never stay in there
and work with him.

00:00:43.133 --> 00:00:46.133
I would always leave out
of the studio and run around

00:00:46.133 --> 00:00:48.968
and do things in the street
and so on and so forth,

00:00:48.968 --> 00:00:50.133
and then I'd come back.

00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:52.334
He'd be like,
"Damn, Pusha! Damn!

00:00:52.334 --> 00:00:54.667
Why don't you just, you know,
just chill with me, man?

00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:57.000
Like, chill with me.
Put everything into the music.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.667
Forget all that other stuff
outside."

00:00:58.667 --> 00:00:59.934
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:00:59.934 --> 00:01:02.000
-So what was -- did you have
a name before that,

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.467
or just your own name?

00:01:03.467 --> 00:01:05.133
-You know, I did.

00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:09.801
Like, before Pusha, right,
it was Terrar.

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:12.467
And it was because
I was born on Friday the 13th

00:01:12.467 --> 00:01:14.467
and yy mother used to call me
Terrence the terror.

00:01:14.467 --> 00:01:16.467
Yeah.
-So, you were a terror?

00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:18.133
-Yeah, yeah. I was pretty bad.

00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:19.634
[ Laughter ]
I was pretty bad.

00:01:19.634 --> 00:01:22.267
-You were bad, yeah?
Yuo were pretty bad, yeah, yeah.

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:24.367
But also, before we get into
the new album --

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:25.868
First of all, congrats.
It's out now.

00:01:25.868 --> 00:01:26.968
We can say it's out now.
-Thank you.

00:01:26.968 --> 00:01:28.133
-"It's Almost Dry."
-Yeah.

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:29.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:29.634 --> 00:01:31.634
That's fresh, too.

00:01:31.634 --> 00:01:35.300
-I want to congratulate you
because you're also a new dad.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:36.968
Buddy, that's what
I'm talking about!

00:01:36.968 --> 00:01:38.300
-Thank you.
-What it's all about, man.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:41.601
-Thank you.
-Great.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:45.434
-Has becoming a dad
changed you at all?

00:01:45.434 --> 00:01:48.601
As a person, as an artist?

00:01:48.601 --> 00:01:51.934
-You know what, it's made me
a lot more focused as an artist

00:01:51.934 --> 00:01:56.934
'cause I feel like now my time
is, like, so precious to me.

00:01:56.934 --> 00:01:59.033
'cause I'm always trying
to get back to my son.

00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:01.267
-Yeah.
-So when I go into the studio,

00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:04.534
it's laser focus, gotta finish,

00:02:04.534 --> 00:02:07.200
gotta, like, get in, get out.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:08.601
'cause I'm trying
to get back home.

00:02:08.601 --> 00:02:09.934
-Yeah. So, it's interesting.

00:02:09.934 --> 00:02:13.434
Yeah, you're a Pusha,
but a different Pusha now.

00:02:13.434 --> 00:02:14.601
-Yeah, for sure.
-Now you're like,

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:15.801
"Let's push this
'cause I gotta go.

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:17.801
Yeah, I gotta go feed the --"
yeah, exactly.

00:02:17.801 --> 00:02:19.300
That's awesome.
I love that.

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:22.634
I gotta say, I love the title.

00:02:22.634 --> 00:02:23.968
"It's Almost Dry."

00:02:23.968 --> 00:02:25.968
Can you explain what the title
means to everyone?

00:02:25.968 --> 00:02:27.801
-Yeah, "It's Almost Dry,"

00:02:27.801 --> 00:02:30.801
it just speaks to trying
to create a masterpiece.

00:02:30.801 --> 00:02:33.801
And as an artist, everybody's
always asking you, like,

00:02:33.801 --> 00:02:36.100
"Man, when you gonna be done?
When's it coming?"

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:37.434
You know, so on and so forth.

00:02:37.434 --> 00:02:40.434
And you always gotta tell them,
like, it's almost ready.

00:02:40.434 --> 00:02:42.601
It's almost dry.
-Yeah, it's almost ready.

00:02:42.601 --> 00:02:44.434
Then we can show the painting
to everybody, yeah.

00:02:44.434 --> 00:02:45.767
-Right, for sure.

00:02:45.767 --> 00:02:49.601
-The entire album is produced
by Pharrell and Kanye.

00:02:49.601 --> 00:02:52.100
-Yeah. Half and half.
It's 12 songs.

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:54.100
Six by Ye, six by Pharrell.

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:57.434
-They must have different
producing styles, I can imagine.

00:02:57.434 --> 00:02:59.267
-Very much so. Very much so.

00:02:59.267 --> 00:03:01.300
-What is Ye like?

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:04.968
-Well, Ye is just
a Pusha T rap fanatic.

00:03:04.968 --> 00:03:07.300
So, he just likes
all of my raps

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:09.801
and he just wants me
to just rap all day long

00:03:09.801 --> 00:03:12.133
and then he just wants to take
them from me and edit them

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:14.634
and do what he wants to do
with it, right?

00:03:14.634 --> 00:03:18.133
Pharrell is like
more of a composer.

00:03:18.133 --> 00:03:22.300
He wants to make sure that
every verse, every hook,

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:25.801
every cadence, every flow,
everything --

00:03:25.801 --> 00:03:28.300
he likes to call them
"sticky moments."

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:30.300
He wants to make sure
that everything is sticky

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:31.801
and just stays with you
the whole time

00:03:31.801 --> 00:03:32.801
throughout the whole song.

00:03:32.801 --> 00:03:34.133
-Is that right?
-Yeah.

00:03:34.133 --> 00:03:35.634
It's way more tedious
with Pharrell.

00:03:35.634 --> 00:03:37.133
It's way tougher with him.

00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:39.467
Way tougher with him.
-That's so good.

00:03:39.467 --> 00:03:41.133
Wow.
I mean, you have great

00:03:41.133 --> 00:03:42.467
collaborations on this,
by the way.

00:03:42.467 --> 00:03:43.968
-Yeah.
-Kid Cudi.

00:03:43.968 --> 00:03:46.467
-Yes.
-You've got Don Toliver.

00:03:46.467 --> 00:03:47.834
-Yep.
-You have Lil Uzi Vert.

00:03:47.834 --> 00:03:49.334
-Yes.
-I love him.

00:03:49.334 --> 00:03:50.834
Jay-Z.
-Yes.

00:03:50.834 --> 00:03:52.334
[ Crowd cheers ]
Yeah.

00:03:52.334 --> 00:03:53.834
-Is it difficult to get...

00:03:53.834 --> 00:03:55.701
How hard is it to get Jay-Z
to do a song?

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:57.868
-Man, it's not that tough.

00:03:57.868 --> 00:03:59.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.367 --> 00:04:01.901
You know, I usually,
I'll just --

00:04:01.901 --> 00:04:04.067
I'll do my parts of a song.

00:04:04.067 --> 00:04:05.734
If I hear a song, hear a beat,

00:04:05.734 --> 00:04:09.234
and I just do everything
I can do to this record,

00:04:09.234 --> 00:04:11.067
but it still needs
something else,

00:04:11.067 --> 00:04:12.400
I'll just email him.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:14.567
Like, I'll email him
and I'll send him the record

00:04:14.567 --> 00:04:16.234
and he'll hit me back like,

00:04:16.234 --> 00:04:18.734
"Man, what the hell
you want me to say to this?"

00:04:18.734 --> 00:04:20.901
-Really?
-And then...

00:04:20.901 --> 00:04:22.567
You know, then he just goes
through this process,

00:04:22.567 --> 00:04:23.901
like every couple days,
he'll be like,

00:04:23.901 --> 00:04:25.901
"Yeah, I got about six lines
for you."

00:04:25.901 --> 00:04:27.100
-Wow!

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.601
-And then, you know,
it just takes a while.

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.267
You know, he goes through it,
and eventually,

00:04:30.267 --> 00:04:31.601
his engineer will call me.

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:34.067
Guru will be like, "Hey,
what's your email address?"

00:04:34.067 --> 00:04:35.734
-Yeah.
-And then I get it back.

00:04:35.734 --> 00:04:37.234
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:04:37.234 --> 00:04:39.734
-On Instagram,
I saw you posted this

00:04:39.734 --> 00:04:42.567
and I was like,
"Oh, could this be something?"

00:04:42.567 --> 00:04:43.734
-Oh, yeah.

00:04:43.734 --> 00:04:45.901
-This is you and Dr. Dre.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:45.901 --> 00:04:47.734
-And, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:47.734 --> 00:04:51.767
[ Applause ]

00:04:51.767 --> 00:04:53.934
-Are you working with Dr. Dre
on something?

00:04:53.934 --> 00:04:56.567
-We actually were just at Nobu.

00:04:56.567 --> 00:04:59.234
His table was across from me.
We were eating.

00:04:59.234 --> 00:05:01.300
And I happened to see him
and I just,

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:03.000
I had to take a picture --
it's Dr. Dre.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:05.234
-[ Laughs ]
So you just went like,

00:05:05.234 --> 00:05:06.567
"Hey, I gotta get a picture,"
just for fun?

00:05:06.567 --> 00:05:07.901
-Yeah, he invited me
to his house, though.

00:05:07.901 --> 00:05:09.567
I'mma go.
I want to go see his house.

00:05:09.567 --> 00:05:11.400
-He invited you to the house?
-Yeah, for sure.

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:12.767
-Oh, really?
-Yeah, I promise.

00:05:12.767 --> 00:05:14.100
-Oh, man. No, I believe it.

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.934
I'm just jealous.

00:05:15.934 --> 00:05:17.667
Yeah, I've known him --
-No, I'm going to see it.

00:05:17.667 --> 00:05:19.000
-No, really?
-Yeah.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.334
-Tell him what's up.
Tell him that --

00:05:20.334 --> 00:05:21.501
-Now you want to see
what his house like.

00:05:21.501 --> 00:05:23.133
-Tell him to email me.
-Yeah, I will.

00:05:23.133 --> 00:05:25.434
[ Laughter ]
-I appreciate it.

00:05:25.434 --> 00:05:27.067
Congratulations
on the album, buddy.

00:05:27.067 --> 00:05:28.734
-Thank you.
-And always come back.

00:05:28.734 --> 00:05:30.567
Come back for the next release
and the next hit.

00:05:30.567 --> 00:05:31.667
-Yes, sir.
-We appreciate it.

00:05:31.667 --> 00:05:33.000
Pusha T, everybody.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:35.300
"It's Almost Dry"
is available now.

